From 063ed769a4ab2d1b92d88b213dec075f37ea2716 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:03:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/38] prefill mmq: pointer-table MMQ (STRATA_MMQ_TAB),
 prep_group, the bitwise test

A Strata-side copy of llama.cpp's MMQ outer scheduler (mul_mat_q, launch_mul_mat_q,
mul_mat_q_switch_J; fallback=false only) in src/prefill/moe_mmq_tab.cuh: each expert's base
address comes from a 16-entry table passed by value instead of x + z * stride_channel_x.
The launch geometry (J, tiles, stream-k grid and k split, fixup) is computed from the same
mmq_args, and process_tile / load_tiles / vec_dot / write_back / the fixup kernel are
upstream's own templates, so the results are the same bits. Instantiated per type from
mmq_tab_instance.cu.in in strata_mmq (same flags); moe_mmq.cu sees declarations only.

CMake turns it off unless the SHA-256 of mmq.cuh's mirrored region (mul_mat_q_process_tile
through mul_mat_q_case) is a verified one: 3cf03257 (the fetched pin; the vendored tree's
mmq.cuh is byte-identical). HIP and SYCL get nothing; Product::tab is a default-null field.

Also: overread_bytes, tab_fits, direct_mode (STRATA_MMQ_DIRECT, read once, 0 unless the tab
is built), direct_slot_guard, and prep_group (one launch: zero the direct experts' guards and
the two group tails). Nothing calls them yet; the default path is unchanged.

tests/cuda/prefill_mmq_tab_test.cu (STRATA_BUILD_TESTS): 874 comparisons on an RTX 3090, all
bitwise identical - IQ3_S gate/up, IQ4_NL and Q8_0 down (1..16 experts, rows
{0,1,7,8,9,31,64,100,512,1000}, every J 8..128, stream-k fixup on and off, max_rows above the
largest count), every other instanced type, mixed direct/gathered groups (compact c != q,
mid-group flush, last entry direct); negative control: guards left as fp16 NaN give non-finite
down outputs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
